OL,3,GNEWSAReform holds on to majority in    
OL,4,Aby-election win                        
OL,6,FReform UK has held on to its majority  
OL,7,Fon a council following a by-election   
OL,8,Fwin.                                   
OL,10,FMark Lee Taylor was elected for Durham 
OL,11,FCounty Council's Craghead and South    
OL,12,FMoor ward on Thursday with 820 votes,  
OL,13,Fbeating Labour's Les Timbey, who       
OL,14,Ffinished second with 728.              
OL,16,FFormer councillor Aaron Hillam's       
OL,17,Fresignation had cut Reform's majority  
OL,18,Fon the local authority to one. It was  
OL,19,F15 when Reform secured 65 seats in     
OL,20,Flocal elections in May 2025.           
OL,23,APub: 20-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
